# Apixaban + 10 DMSO: XTB2 geometry optimization
# Starting geometry: final frame (Step 20000, t=20 ps) of the confined XTB2 MD
#   trajectory Apixaban_10DMSO_XTB_preequil_confined.xyz
#   (Cell Sphere confinement, r=14.0 Ang)
#
# Purpose: relax the MD snapshot to its nearest XTB2 local minimum, removing
#   the thermal/kinetic-energy strain present in the raw MD frame, before
#   further use (e.g. as a starting point for r2SCAN-3c work, or for a cleaner
#   XTB2-level energy comparison). Analogous to
#   Apixaban/Water/MD/XTB2Opt/Apixaban_10H2O_XTB2_Opt_from_confined_final.inp.
#
# Note: no SMD/solvent model and no Cell/confinement here - this is a plain
#   gas-phase XTB2 Opt of the whole 159-atom snapshot (Apixaban + 10 explicit
#   DMSO), so the DMSO molecules are free to move; some may drift apart during
#   optimization since there is no confining potential in this run.

! XTB2 Opt

%pal
  nprocs 4
end

%maxcore 2000

